+Booting through Open Firmware
+-----------------------------
+
+QEMU's `-kernel` loader places a segment at its load address plus 16 MiB,
+so the default link uses load addresses starting at zero. Open Firmware
+loads an ELF image at its load addresses; link images for it with
+
+```shell
+-Wl,--defsym=IBOOKG3_LOAD_BASE=0x01000000
+```
+
+and put them on an HFS+ volume, for example a CD with an Apple partition
+map, then at the Open Firmware prompt: `boot cd:3,\rtems.elf`.
+
