@@ -80,9 +98,12 @@ configuration of the tester.
 Limitations
 -----------
 
-* Only tested on QEMU. Booting on real hardware needs a loader path from
-  Open Firmware (for example from disk) that places the image at 16 MiB.
-* No framebuffer console; the real iBook has no external serial port.
+* Only tested on QEMU. Booting through Open Firmware's own ELF loader from
+  a CD (Apple partition map + HFS+) works on QEMU's OpenBIOS; Apple's Open
+  Firmware is not tested.
+* Console input only from the ESCC, which the real iBook does not bring
+  out; the built-in keyboard is on the PMU (not supported), a USB keyboard
+  works through rtems-libbsd.
 * No PMU support (power off, real-time clock, battery).
 * The KeyLargo ATA driver runs in PIO mode; DMA modes are untested.
